Neural Decoding and Brain-Computer Interfaces (append to existing):                                                  

Recent advances in brain-to-language decoding have expanded... [^2609.27650]... [^10.7273_000007929].                

New additions:                                                                                                       

Brain-to-image retrieval systems are also evolving rapidly, with NeuroGlyph learning a trial-independent visual      
target across multiple depths of a frozen visual backbone to outperform final-layer supervision on THINGS-EEG and    
THINGS-MEG datasets [^2609.24136]. To address spatial mixing in scalp EEG, adaptive cortically constrained alignment 
methods reconstruct responses into ROI-level source patterns, achieving strong zero-shot retrieval performance while 
providing post hoc interpretability [^2609.24109]. For language decoding, Hierarchical Dynamic Neural Decoding (HDND)
treats word retrieval as structured refinement, combining intermediate neural representations and contextual semantic
predictions to yield higher balanced Top-10 estimates across seven EEG and MEG datasets in multiple languages        
[^2609.24095]. Auditing EEG foundation models on motor imagery reveals that foundation models and task-specific      
decoders evaluated with matched input pipelines show architecture-dependent accuracy differences, highlighting the   
need for standardized evaluation protocols [^2609.23924]. In clinical monitoring, chaotic dynamics-regulated         
topological learning partitions EEG signals into discrete functional subnets and models nodes as Lorenz oscillators  
to reliably distinguish preictal from interictal states in patient-specific networks [^2609.23317]. Large-scale      
neural recording benchmarks like BrainWideBench demonstrate that pretraining on multi-region recordings from hundreds
of mice improves cross-animal transfer for decoding behavior and predicting masked neural activity, though gains     
remain highly dependent on objective alignment [^2609.22064]. Furthermore, proactive AI assistance systems like      
PV-Care integrate wearable EEG with visual environmental perception to detect cognitive states (Learning, Memory     
Recall, Resting) in Mild Cognitive Impairment patients, generating context-aware prompts for large language models to
deliver real-time voice assistance [^2609.22024].                                                                    

Computational Neuroimaging and Foundation Models (append to existing):                                               

... [^2609.26512]... [^2609.27256].                                                                                  

New additions:                                                                                                       

Foundational architectures are being adapted for brain-specific challenges, such as Brain-Inspired Hierarchical      
Modularity, which coordinates continual learning through expert specialization and ensemble integration inspired by  
the Drosophila learning system, consistently improving performance under online and uncertain data streams across    
vision and embodied tasks [^2609.25146]. Evaluating neuroimaging foundation models on underrepresented cohorts       
reveals that frozen backbones often collapse to majority-class predictions on non-western clinical brain MRI         
datasets, underscoring the need for parameter-efficient adaptation and broader external validation [^2609.23983]. At 
the network topology level, scalable generative frameworks superimposing metric decay with latent functional geometry
successfully reconstruct hidden node coordinates in the Drosophila whole-brain connectome, uncovering an             
architectural hierarchy from sensory peripheries to associative neuropils [^2609.23933]. Functional connectivity     
analysis is being reformulated through edge-centric brain transformers that construct edge time-series               
representations to capture dynamic co-fluctuation patterns, organizing discriminative connections into line graphs   
for explicit connection-to-connection modeling in rs-fMRI [^2609.23782]. For cellular reconstruction, SomaNet employs
a teacher-student paradigm with affinity learning to achieve accurate, weakly supervised 3D electron microscopy soma 
instance segmentation under partial annotation constraints [^2609.23019]. Training efficiency for latent world models
is also being optimized; Mask-Aware JEPA execution separates mask-independent computation from routing, reducing     
memory traffic and achieving up to 1.7x speedup for brain dynamics and time series training [^2609.22674]. Medical   
imaging synthesis benefits from AWR-Net, which decouples anatomical correspondence from ultrasound appearance using  
wavelet diffusion and residual refinement to generate realistic 3D fetal brain volumes from MRI label maps           
[^2609.22635]. Unsupervised anomaly detection frameworks validated on brain MRI benchmarks achieve strong detection  
performance by inferring corruption parameters as probabilistic anomaly scores, producing estimates of pathology     
intensity and geometry [^2609.21800]. Submillimeter fMRI reliability is enhanced by Voxel-Matching NORDIC, which     
gathers similar non-local voxels based on time-series similarity to boost signal redundancy and significantly improve
temporal SNR without inducing excessive spatial smoothness [^2609.21517]. Accelerated brain MRI acquisition is       
improved by Anatomy-aware Residual Attention Networks that refine SENSE reconstructions through generalized          
self-attention, preserving anatomical fidelity for quantitative measurements [^2609.22390]. Finally, forecasting     
intrathecal tracer enhancement from pre-contrast brain MRI demonstrates that direct image-to-image regression        
outperforms conditional flow matching in accuracy and computational cost, predicting enhancement from anatomy and    
timing alone [^2609.22377].                                                                                          

Neurodegenerative Disorders and Brain Tumors (append to existing):                                                   

