New additions:                                                                                                       

Automated tumor segmentation continues to advance with VGG16-MCA UNet, which pairs an ImageNet-pretrained encoder    
with a decoder-side multi-channel attention module to achieve high pixel-level Dice scores for whole-tumor           
segmentation in 2D FLAIR MRI [^2609.23919]. Interactive 3D lesion segmentation is being enhanced by BrainIAC, a      
unified framework integrating multi-modal backends, bounding-box/click prompts, and online adaptation mechanisms that
generalize across heterogeneous imaging modalities and unseen pathologies [^2609.23026]. Survival prediction for     
glioblastoma multiforme is improved by a multi-modal framework combining sheaf hypergraph neural networks for        
higher-order tissue patch relationships, concept bottleneck layers for ante-hoc interpretability, and extension      
sufficiency test regularization to ensure faithful explanations [^2609.25088]. Clinical gait analysis and            
neurodegenerative disease monitoring benefit from diagonal segment extraction techniques that transform dynamic time 
warping into an interpretable tool for localizing coordination breakdowns [^2609.24223]. In Parkinson's disease,     
implanted neurostimulators storing local field potentials face quantization artifacts that corrupt spectral          
biomarkers; dequantization via interval-censored subspace estimation reduces spurious peak detection while preserving
true oscillatory activity [^2609.22658]. Post-cardiac arrest neuroprotection is explored through artemisinin         
treatment, which alleviates hippocampal neuronal apoptosis and cognitive dysfunction in rats by modulating the       
PI3K/Akt signaling pathway [^10.36721_pjps.2026.39.12.334.1]. The cellular architecture of breast cancer brain       
metastases is being mapped using multimodal tissue cytometry and spatial transcriptomics, revealing prognostically   
distinct immune niches that inform personalized treatment strategies [^10.5281_zenodo.17723783]. Drug delivery across
the blood-brain barrier is being advanced through medical microbubbles combined with ultrasound, offering potential  
for targeted gene therapy and cancer treatment [^10.5281_zenodo.19676283]. Clinical outcomes for brain metastases    
from colorectal cancer treated with stereotactic radiosurgery show higher local failure rates compared to other      
primaries, highlighting the radioresistant biology of this histology [^10.1093_nop_npag050]. Environmental factors   
are also linked to neurodegeneration, as differential DNA methylation in blood mediates the association between      
ambient PM2.5 exposure and cerebrospinal fluid biomarkers of Alzheimer's disease [^10.1038_s41380-026-03662-9].      
Stereotactic radiosurgery for thalamic brain metastases demonstrates sufficient local control and high survival rates
over time, supporting its role as an effective treatment option [^10.1227_neuprac.0000000000000284]. Preoperative    
frailty measures for vestibular schwannoma surgeries indicate that tumor size, rather than frailty indices, is the   
dominant correlate of early postoperative outcomes like length of stay and facial nerve function                     
[^10.1227_neuprac.0000000000000289].                                                                                 

