Section 1: Neural Decoding and Brain-Computer Interfaces                                                             

Existing ends with: ...investigate early self-regulation and emotional reactivity [^10.7273_000007929].              

Append: `Brain-to-image retrieval systems are also evolving rapidly, with NeuroGlyph learning a trial-independent    
visual target across multiple depths of a frozen visual backbone to outperform final-layer supervision on THINGS-EEG 
and THINGS-MEG datasets [^2609.24136]. To address spatial mixing in scalp EEG, adaptive cortically constrained       
alignment methods reconstruct responses into ROI-level source patterns, achieving strong zero-shot retrieval         
performance while providing post hoc interpretability [^2609.24109]. For language decoding, Hierarchical Dynamic     
Neural Decoding (HDND) treats word retrieval as structured refinement, combining intermediate neural representations 
and contextual semantic predictions to yield higher balanced Top-10 estimates across seven EEG and MEG datasets in   
multiple languages [^2609.24095]. Auditing EEG foundation models on motor imagery reveals that foundation models and 
task-specific decoders evaluated with matched input pipelines show architecture-dependent accuracy differences,      
highlighting the need for standardized evaluation protocols [^2609.23924]. In clinical monitoring, chaotic           
dynamics-regulated topological learning partitions EEG signals into discrete functional subnets and models nodes as  
Lorenz oscillators to reliably distinguish preictal from interictal states in patient-specific networks              
[^2609.23317]. Large-scale neural recording benchmarks like BrainWideBench demonstrate that pretraining on           
multi-region recordings from hundreds of mice improves cross-animal transfer for decoding behavior and predicting    
masked neural activity, though gains remain highly dependent on objective alignment [^2609.22064]. Furthermore,      
proactive AI assistance systems like PV-Care integrate wearable EEG with visual environmental perception to detect   
cognitive states (Learning, Memory Recall, Resting) in Mild Cognitive Impairment patients, generating context-aware  
prompts for large language models to deliver real-time voice assistance [^2609.22024].                               

