multi-region recordings from hundreds of mice improves cross-animal transfer for decoding behavior and predicting    
masked neural activity, though gains remain highly dependent on objective alignment [^2609.22064]. Furthermore,      
proactive AI assistance systems like PV-Care integrate wearable EEG with visual environmental perception to detect   
cognitive states (Learning, Memory Recall, Resting) in Mild Cognitive Impairment patients, generating context-aware  
prompts for large language models to deliver real-time voice assistance [^2609.22024].                               
                                                                                                                     
 ## Computational Neuroimaging and Foundation Models                                                                 
                                                                                                                     
-The integration of foundation models and scalable simulation is transforming structural and functional neuroimaging.
BrainFedFM introduces a dual-priority federated pretraining strategy for structural brain MRI, achieving             
state-of-the-art performance across diverse classification and segmentation tasks without pooling raw images         
[^2609.27611]. At the mechanistic level, CerebroSim enables scalable whole-brain spiking simulation at the           
100-trillion-synapse scale on supercomputers, utilizing delay-aware spike broadcast and sparse synapse storage       
compression to make biologically constrained human-brain models practical for disorder studies [^2609.27482]. Image  
reconstruction techniques are also advancing rapidly; Directional Total Variation-Regularized Implicit Neural        
Representations (DTV-INR) integrate coordinate-driven networks with anisotropic regularizers to achieve continuous   
super-resolution in clinical brain MRI, circumventing staircasing artifacts [^2609.25429]. Similarly,                
uncertainty-aware 3D residual wavelet diffusion models address memory bottlenecks in ultra low-field MRI             
super-resolution, generating per-voxel uncertainty maps that highlight anatomical ambiguity while preserving         
disease-relevant atrophy [^2609.25319]. Motion correction in magnetic resonance fingerprinting has been enhanced by  
compact spiral navigators, enabling sub-second motion estimation and improving quantitative map reliability under    
rapid, unpredictable motion [^2609.25313]. Methodologically, additive nonparametric regression frameworks            
incorporating Gaussian process priors effectively predict task-based brain activation maps by modeling intricate     
functional dependencies between structural, resting-state, and task-fMRI data [^2609.26867]. In developmental        
contexts, deep learning is shifting infant functional neuroimaging from group-level analyses toward reliable,        
individualized trajectory forecasting [^2609.26688]. Comparative studies using EEG encoding models reveal that vision
transformers sustain brain-predictive correspondence at deeper network layers better than CNNs, largely due to       
preserved patch-token representations [^2609.26512]. Additionally, functional causal discovery via conditional       
covariance ordering provides a distribution-free approach to estimating brain effective connectivity directed acyclic
graphs [^2609.27256].                                                                                                
