 ## Neurodegenerative Disorders and Brain Tumors                                                                     
                                                                                                                     
-Understanding and treating brain pathologies continues to drive methodological innovation. Low-level blast exposure 
in veterans has been linked to statistically significant increases in depression and mental health symptoms,         
independent of PTSD or alcohol use, suggesting cumulative overpressure accelerates neurodegenerative or affective    
decline [^2609.25279]. Automated segmentation of brain metastases, which are often small and heterogeneous, benefits 
from multi-architecture comparisons; transformer-based models like Primus and residual encoder variants show         
complementary strengths in aggregate Dice scores versus lesion-wise F1 metrics [^2609.24769]. Unsupervised anomaly   
detection in medical scans is being reformulated as a Bayesian inverse problem with diffusion priors, jointly        
inferring pseudo-healthy images and spatial anomaly masks to improve localization on FDG PET and FLAIR MRI           
[^2609.24265]. In Alzheimer's disease research, the amyloid precursor protein (APP) is increasingly viewed as a      
universal pro-survival molecule rather than merely a pathological substrate, raising critical questions about the    
safety of broad-spectrum APP suppression therapies [^10.5281_zenodo.20049820]. Liquid biopsy approaches for          
glioblastoma multiforme (GBM) are advancing through cfDNA analysis; nucleosome repositioning landscapes and          
repeat-based cfDNA profiling offer non-invasive diagnostic signatures that mirror tumor-specific chromatin           
reprogramming [^10.5526_err-00042862][^10.5526_err-00042900]. Spatially resolved single-cell datasets for pan-cancer 
brain metastases have been released to facilitate microenvironment mapping                                           
[^10.5281_zenodo.21816284][^10.5281_zenodo.21782885]. Therapeutic delivery across the blood-brain barrier is being   
addressed via lipid nanoparticle formulations encapsulating siRNA targeting TERT or loaded with anticancer           
phytochemicals, demonstrating robust gene silencing and cytotoxic effects in GBM cell lines                          
[^10.17030_uclan.thesis.00059253][^10.17030_uclan.thesis.00059033]. Furthermore, RET signaling pathways have been    
identified as mediators of estrogen receptor-positive breast cancer brain metastasis [^10.5281_zenodo.19501083],     
while secretomes and extracellular vesicles from neural crest-derived stem cells show promise in inhibiting GBM      
proliferation and modulating inflammatory microenvironments [^10.48683_1926.00128572]. Finally, aerobic exercise is  
proposed to reshape nitric oxide signaling toward adaptive profiles that may enhance mitophagy and provide           
neuroprotection in Parkinson's disease [^10.4103_mgr.medgasres-d-26-00008].                                          
