 ## Cognitive Neuroscience and Developmental Dynamics                                                                
                                                                                                                     
-Cognitive and developmental frameworks are being enriched by computational and molecular insights. AI-driven neural 
surrogate frameworks combine fMRI decoding with constrained latent-space steering to propose and test predicted      
perceptual effects for cognitive-affective neuromodulation, offering a falsifiable upstream method for designing     
psychiatric intervention targets [^2609.27729]. The concept of task-based neurons challenges traditional architecture
designs, arguing that customized neurons capture task-specific prior knowledge; the TNLearn package facilitates      
automated construction and training of these networks [^2609.27564]. Theoretical models also explore emotions as     
intrinsic colored noise in biological networks, demonstrating how decision dynamics and opinion formation shift under
varying imitation effects and memory ranges [^2609.25970]. Clinical gait analysis benefits from diagonal segment     
extraction from dynamic time warping paths, transforming DTW into an interpretable tool for localizing coordination  
breakdowns in neurodegenerative diseases [^2609.24223]. Cross-cultural and aging studies reveal that category fluency
performance is shaped by both gray matter volume variations in semantic control regions and culturally distinct      
cognitive categorization strategies [^10.48617_etd.1671]. In motor control, brain-based digital twins fuse EEG with  
kinematic data to model skilled interceptive movements, providing real-time neural efficiency feedback through       
synthetic data augmentation and closed-loop intervention [^10.17870_bathspa.00017805]. At the molecular level,       
circular RNAs accumulate in the Drosophila brain at rates corresponding to biological age, serving as stable         
biomarkers of the aging process and insulin-related pathways [^10.48617_etd.1568]. Systemic metabolism also          
intersects with brain function, as arteriovenous metabolomics profiling reveals significant organ-specific uptake and
release of circulating metabolites, including those relevant to cerebral physiology [^10.5281_zenodo.20652506].      
+Cognitive and developmental frameworks are being enriched by computational and molecular insights. AI-driven neural 
surrogate frameworks combine fMRI decoding with constrained latent-space steering to propose and test predicted      
perceptual effects for cognitive-affective neuromodulation, offering a falsifiable upstream method for designing     
psychiatric intervention targets [^2609.27729]. The concept of task-based neurons challenges traditional architecture
designs, arguing that customized neurons capture task-specific prior knowledge; the TNLearn package facilitates      
automated construction and training of these networks [^2609.27564]. Theoretical models also explore emotions as     
intrinsic colored noise in biological networks, demonstrating how decision dynamics and opinion formation shift under
varying imitation effects and memory ranges [^2609.25970]. Cross-cultural and aging studies reveal that category     
fluency performance is shaped by both gray matter volume variations in semantic control regions and culturally       
distinct cognitive categorization strategies [^10.48617_etd.1671]. In motor control, brain-based digital twins fuse  
EEG with kinematic data to model skilled interceptive movements, providing real-time neural efficiency feedback      
through synthetic data augmentation and closed-loop intervention [^10.17870_bathspa.00017805]. At the molecular      
level, circular RNAs accumulate in the Drosophila brain at rates corresponding to biological age, serving as stable  
biomarkers of the aging process and insulin-related pathways [^10.48617_etd.1568]. Systemic metabolism also          
intersects with brain function, as arteriovenous metabolomics profiling reveals significant organ-specific uptake and
release of circulating metabolites, including those relevant to cerebral physiology [^10.5281_zenodo.20652506].      
                                                                                                                     
 ## Neural Signaling and Circuit Mechanisms                                                                          
                                                                                                                     
-Fundamental circuit mechanisms continue to be elucidated through targeted signaling studies. Cholecystokinin (CCK)  
signaling in the nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS) plays a critical role in satiety and energy balance; NTS-CCK    
neurons are directly connected to vagal afferents and can release local CCK to activate downstream neurons, with     
high-fat diets shown to blunt central CCK signaling in males [^10.7273_000008411]. Olfactory system organization is  
also being redefined, revealing that each olfactory receptor is expressed at a unique mean dorsoventral position in  
the epithelium, instantiating a stereotyped receptor map that aligns sensory maps in the nose and brain through a    
coherent gene expression program [^10.5281_zenodo.18941307].                                                         
+Fundamental circuit mechanisms continue to be elucidated through targeted signaling studies. Cholecystokinin (CCK)  
signaling in the nucleus of the solitary tract (NTS) plays a critical role in satiety and energy balance; NTS-CCK    
neurons are directly connected to vagal afferents and can release local CCK to activate downstream neurons, with     
high-fat diets shown to blunt central CCK signaling in males [^10.7273_000008411]. Olfactory system organization is  
also being redefined, revealing that each olfactory receptor is expressed at a unique mean dorsoventral position in  
the epithelium, instantiating a stereotyped receptor map that aligns sensory maps in the nose and brain through a    
coherent gene expression program [^10.5281_zenodo.18941307]. Generative modeling of neural population activity is    
advancing through discrete models that represent array-wide spiking activity using a shared vocabulary of            
spatiotemporal motifs learned via residual vector-quantized autoencoders, achieving superior reconstruction and      
generation metrics without assay-specific parameters [^2609.23907].                                                  
                                                                                                                     

